- Idea Kind
    |Kind                                     |how to recognise                                                                             |expression                     |purpose                                                                                                                                                                                                |extra Rules                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |example                    |said of (S)   |present in (P)|
    |-----------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------------------------+--------------+--------------|
    |**Example** (Individual Substance)       |A `- ` (dash + space) child, **or** the `value` in a capitalised `Concept: value` line       |Indent Dash prefix after a term|one record type with a fixed number of attributes                                                                                                                                                      |`- Socrates`, or `Run Command: code --install …`    A `Concept: value` line is the same shorthand on the Substance side. The capitalised term stays an ordinary **Concept**; `value` is one Example of it — exactly what a `- value` child would be — written inline as a convenient first Example. The inheritance runs **Concept → Example**, just as with a dashed child. Like any Example, the inline one inherits **all** of the Concept's attributes *and* their values (defaults) — the value (`code --install`) is the Example's own identity, and everything the Concept defines accrues to that Example instance, exactly as for a `- ` child. The inheritance is the Example's, not the Concept's. Further Examples may follow as ordinary `- ` children below it, and the Concept may still divide into **sub-Concepts**, each with Examples of its own — the inline value is simply one Example among however many the Concept comes to have. Model data as sets of using Examples|`Human` indent `- Socrates`|**False (~S)**|**False (~P)**|
    |**Concept** (Universal Substance)        |First letter is capitalised                                                                  |Indent Concept under a term    |Defines a class or type of idea                                                                                                                                                                        |A Concept may reappear elsewhere only if a distinguishing qualifier prefix makes it unique. A sub-Concept is an **is-a**, never a **has-a**. Indenting one Concept under another asserts the child *is a kind of* the parent. "And" (always split the function into two siblings). Start two levels of granularity above the detail you need, then prune until every leaf is directly executable. Remove anything that does not serve the model. Prioritise Concepts by relevance                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |`Mammal` indent `Human`    |**True (S)**  |**False (~P)**|
    |**Attribute** (Universal Accident)       |All lowercase                                                                                |Indent attribute under a term  |Defines a property that a Concept has                                                                                                                                                                  |Every attribute is itself a Concept that can be expanded on somewhere else, whether or not it is defined elsewhere. Non-nullable attributes listed first; attribute order otherwise meaningless                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |`Human` indent `is alive`  |**True (S)**  |**True (P)**  |
    |**Attribute Value** (Individual Accident)|The `value` after the colon in `attribute: value`; the term before the colon is **lowercase**|Colon after a term             |The concrete value an attribute takes. An `attribute: value` line is **two** ideas — the attribute (`colour`) and the value (`red`) that descends from it — written on one line, not one combined thing|`colour: red` (the value `red`, under the attribute `colour`)       An `attribute: value` line is shorthand for **two** ideas, not one. `colour: red` says the attribute `colour` — a universal accident the Concept *has* — takes the individual value `red`. The inheritance runs **Concept/Example → attribute → value**: the value descends from its attribute, and the attribute from the idea that carries it. The value never descends from the Example directly, and `colour` is not part of the value's name — the attribute and its value merely share a line. Remove attributes that do not serve the model                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |`is alive: No`             |**False (~S)**|**True (P)**  |
